The deterministic adapter qualification creates a temporary local bare Git remote. It explicitly
enables local-repository publication only inside the fixture and verifies the exact single-parent
commit, temporary-index crash safety, idempotent local-ref reuse, lease-guarded feature-branch
creation, divergent-ref rejection, symbolic/ref-history override and metadata-path escape rejection,
isolated Git configuration, worktree/index drift rejection, exact retry
reconciliation, completed receipt replay after sandbox cleanup, stable adapter/Draft-PR identity
binding, optional Draft-PR binding, and the default-disabled adapter loader. It does not use hosted
credentials, contact a hosted source-control provider, or modify the checked-out source repository.

Publication is a separate action after `safe-publish-resume`; approval never triggers it
automatically. Read `publish_approval_sha256` and `publish_patch_sha256` from the completed task's
`safe-final-report.json`, then explicitly configure a trusted adapter factory and select exactly one
action:

```bash
